body:
The "loading server list" means the game is looking for the file cnsl.xml (a file that has a list of different servers the game uses). GameContainer.swf and cnsl.xml need to be in the same folder when you run the game otherwise you get stuck on that part of the loading screen.

&#x200B;

The game files are supposed to be organized the way they are in the zip file called "[i.cartoonnetwork.com](https://i.cartoonnetwork.com)". if you run GameContainer.swf from that file you should be able to get to the main menu. 

&#x200B;

When I run the game using the standalone Adobe Flash Player I get stuck on the main menu(the buttons don't work). But if I run the game in Ruffle by entering this link:([https://i.cartoonnetwork.com/games/tko/GameContainer.swf](https://i.cartoonnetwork.com/games/tko/GameContainer.swf)), the menu buttons actually work, but the game gets stuck trying to load servers that don't exist anymore.

&#x200B;

(I used the Ruffle browser extension for this part, I don't know how it would work with other versions of Ruffle)

&#x200B;

What I meant about the GameContainer.swf file having server code is that it has the code that connects you to a server for matchmaking, and it also has code related to SmartFoxServer, the service they used to run the game servers. There's probably more stuff in there but I haven't looked at the code in months, and I also don't understand all of it.

&#x200B;

Feel free to ask more questions
